@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Session — who does what?
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontColor #0F172A
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 16
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #CBD5E1
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
top to bottom direction
rectangle "SCREEN\nCalls useSession()" as Screen #DBEAFE
rectangle "CONTEXT\nSessionProvider supplies one session object\nuseSession subscribes and reads" as Context #DBEAFE
rectangle "AUTH CONTROLLER\nCoordinates login, refresh and logout" as Auth #EDE9FE
rectangle "SESSION STORE\nCurrent user, status and error\nPrivate access token + version counter" as Store #DCFCE7
rectangle "CREDENTIAL STORAGE\nNative: SecureStore\nWeb: HttpOnly cookie + local marker" as Storage #FEF3C7
rectangle "BACKEND\nValidates credentials\nIssues / revokes refresh credentials" as Backend #F1F5F9
Screen --> Context : Read state / call actions
Context --> Store : Subscribe and read
Context --> Auth : Direct session methods
Auth --> Store : Commit or clear
Auth --> Storage : Read / write via adapter
Auth --> Backend : Login / refresh / logout
note bottom of Store
Each browser tab has its own store.
sessionSync announces changes between tabs.
end note
@enduml
